---
import Layout from "../../layouts/Layout.astro";
import { site } from "../../data.mjs";
import BubbleMailerGuideImages from "../../components/BubbleMailerGuideImages.astro";
import BubbleMailerMeasurements from "../../components/BubbleMailerMeasurements.astro";
const path = "/guides/kraft-vs-poly-bubble-mailers/";
const title = "Kraft Bubble Mailers vs Poly Bubble Mailers";
const schema = { "@context": "https://schema.org", "@type": "Article", headline: title, author: { "@type": "Organization", name: "Welltroy" }, publisher: { "@type": "Organization", name: "Welltroy" }, mainEntityOfPage: `${site.origin}${path}`, datePublished: "2026-10-20", dateModified: "2026-11-08" };
const breadcrumbs = { "@context": "https://schema.org", "@type": "BreadcrumbList", itemListElement: [{ "@type": "ListItem", position: 1, name: "Home", item: site.origin }, { "@type": "ListItem", position: 2, name: "Buying Guide", item: `${site.origin}/guides/choose-a-mailer/` }, { "@type": "ListItem", position: 3, name: "Kraft vs poly bubble mailers", item: `${site.origin}${path}` }] };
---
<Layout title={`${title} | Welltroy`} description="Compare paper-exterior kraft bubble mailers with poly bubble mailers by appearance, published sizes, usable inner space, printing and packing tests before requesting a quote." canonicalPath={path} schemas={[schema, breadcrumbs]}>
  <section class="page-hero bubble-guide-hero"><div class="container"><div class="breadcrumbs"><a href="/">Home</a> / <a href="/guides/choose-a-mailer/">Buying Guide</a> / Kraft vs poly bubble mailers</div><p class="eyebrow">Protective mailer comparison</p><h1>{title}</h1><p class="lead">Start with a kraft bubble mailer if a paper exterior suits your presentation, or a poly bubble mailer if you want a flexible film exterior and a published range of outer sizes to shortlist. In either case, the bubble construction, usable inner space, seal and full shipping pack must be confirmed for your actual item. The exterior alone does not establish protection or recyclability.</p><p class="muted">By Welltroy · Updated <time datetime="2026-11-08">8 November 2026</time></p><nav class="anchor-links" aria-label="In this guide"><a href="#compare">Compare</a><a href="#usable-size">Inner &amp; outer size</a><a href="#example">Size example</a><a href="#film-and-liner">Film &amp; liner</a><a href="#test">Test</a><a href="#quote">Quote brief</a></nav></div></section>
  <section class="section"><div class="container article-layout"><article class="article-main">
    <h2 id="compare">What Changes When the Exterior Changes?</h2>
    <BubbleMailerGuideImages />
    <div class="table-wrap" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label="Kraft and poly bubble mailer comparison"><table><thead><tr><th>Decision point</th><th>Yellow kraft bubble mailer</th><th>Poly bubble mailer</th></tr></thead><tbody>
      <tr><td>Shown construction</td><td>Yellow kraft paper exterior with bubble lining</td><td>Flexible film exterior with internal bubble cushioning</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Presentation</td><td>Paper appearance; confirm paper weight and print result</td><td>Film appearance; confirm exterior color and print method</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Published size information</td><td>No numbered size table on the current product page; request both outer and usable inner dimensions</td><td>15 catalogue outer sizes, BM01–BM15; usable inner dimensions still need confirmation</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Protection</td><td>Confirm bubble structure and test the packed item</td><td>Confirm bubble structure and test the packed item</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Closure and artwork</td><td>Peel-and-seal flap shown; confirm adhesive and print placement</td><td>Confirm flap, adhesive, exterior finish and printable area for the chosen model</td></tr>
    </tbody></table></div>
    <p><a href="/products/kraft-padded-mailers/">Plain Kraft Padded Mailers</a> are another paper-exterior option, but their lining structure is selected per specification; do not assume it is identical to the yellow kraft bubble style. Ask for construction details before comparing quotations.</p>
    <div class="guide-callout"><strong>A branded poly bubble mailer in practice.</strong><p>The LUMIÈRE project pairs a matte pink exterior with black brand artwork and bubble cushioning. <a href="/products/poly-bubble-mailers/#lumiere-case">Explore the LUMIÈRE customer project →</a>, then confirm the construction and usable space for your own item. The boxed-accessory size example below describes a separate hypothetical pack.</p></div>
    <h2 id="usable-size">Are Bubble Mailer Sizes Internal or External?</h2>
    <p><strong>Check the stated measurement basis before comparing sizes.</strong> Welltroy BM-series catalogue dimensions are outer width × body length + a separate flap. The space inside the liner and seams is a different measurement; it must be confirmed for the selected construction.</p>
    <BubbleMailerMeasurements />
    <p>For an illustrative request, “minimum 12 × 16 inches usable inner space” means a target of 30.48 × 40.64 cm inside, not a catalogue outer size. This conversion does not identify a Welltroy stock model or prove that a thick packed item fits. Keep the original units and inner-size requirement in the written brief.</p>
    <p>Request the supplier's measurement method, usable opening and agreed tolerance. Then insert the complete packed item and close the flap. Do not subtract a fixed liner allowance from every exterior size: construction and contents vary. Use the <a href="/products/poly-bubble-mailers/#specification-checks">poly bubble specification checks</a> to request these details.</p>
    <h2 id="example">Worked Size Example: A Boxed Accessory</h2>
    <p>Suppose an accessory in its retail box measures 20 × 24 × 3 cm. The <a href="/products/poly-bubble-mailers/">Poly Bubble Mailers</a> catalogue lists BM08 as 25 × 30 + 5 cm and BM10 as 29 × 36 + 5 cm, both outer width × length + flap. BM08 may be too tight once the 3 cm thickness, bubble lining and seams are considered; BM10 is a larger candidate to ask about. Neither outer size proves a fit. Request usable internal width and length, then insert and seal a real sample.</p>
    <p>The current <a href="/products/yellow-kraft-bubble-mailers/">Yellow Kraft Bubble Mailers</a> page does not list numbered sizes. Send the same packed dimensions and ask for a comparable kraft option with its outer and usable inner measurements. Compare quotations for the same packing requirement and quantity rather than treating unlike model names as equivalent.</p>
    <h2 id="film-and-liner">What Thickness Should I Specify for a Bubble Mailer?</h2>
    <p>Describe the outer layer and the cushioning layer separately. For a poly exterior, ask whether the quoted thickness is single-wall film gauge and state the unit. For kraft, ask for the paper weight. Record the bubble-liner construction and any overall-bag measurement separately; these values describe different parts of the bag.</p>
    <p>A thicker film number does not, by itself, establish better cushioning or protection for a fragile product. Include the retail box, packed weight, sharp edges and handling concerns so the proposed liner, seams, closure and any additional outer packaging can be reviewed together.</p>
    <h2 id="test">Test the Complete Pack, Not Just the Mailer</h2>
    <ul><li>Check insertion, seam tension, flap closure and label placement with the actual packed product.</li><li>Test handling and transit conditions relevant to your shipment. For fragile, heavy, sharp or crushable goods, a mailer may need additional protection or a box.</li><li>If moisture exposure matters, ask for a material-specific test or protective solution. Do not infer water resistance from paper or film appearance alone.</li><li>For environmental claims, request the exact material and liner documentation and check the intended disposal route in the destination market. A paper exterior with bubble lining is not automatically recyclable.</li></ul>
    <p>Use the <a href="/guides/custom-mailer-sample-approval/#bubble-sample-trial">five-point bubble sample check map</a> to keep the fit, seams, closure, printing and label checks together. Record accepted items, required changes and pending checks separately.</p>
    <h2 id="quote">Request Comparable Samples and Quotes</h2>
    <p>Send the item and packed dimensions, weight, shipping route, target quantity per size and design, preferred exterior, required cushioning, artwork and destination. Ask for the inner measurements, paper or film specification, bubble structure, seal, sample arrangements and quotation for each candidate. If printing is involved, use our <a href="/guides/logo-artwork-checklist/">logo artwork checklist</a> to prepare files and placement notes.</p>
    <p>For a matte color, metallic reflection or holographic effect, use the <a href="/guides/metallic-vs-holographic-bubble-mailers/#matte-colors">bubble mailer finish guide</a> to separate appearance from construction.</p>
    <p>For a paper-exterior bubble option, <a href="/products/yellow-kraft-bubble-mailers/#quote-brief">build a Kraft Bubble Mailer brief</a> with your size targets, paper and lining questions, closure, artwork, quantity and destination. Your requests remain editable before sending.</p>
    <p><a class="text-link" href="/downloads/bubble-mailer-quote-brief.txt" download>Download the updated bubble mailer quote and sample brief (.txt) ↓</a></p>
    <p>When comparing quantity tiers, keep the construction and artwork the same. Confirm unit and setup costs, sample courier charges, carton details and the bulk delivery scope for your destination. See the <a href="/guides/metallic-vs-holographic-bubble-mailers/#delivered-quote">quantity and delivered-quote checklist</a> and the <a href="/guides/compare-custom-mailer-quotes/">supplier quote worksheet</a>.</p>
    <div class="button-row"><a class="button" href="/quote/?product=multiple-products#quote-form" data-quote-placement="content">Compare Kraft and Poly Options</a><a class="text-link" href="/products/poly-bubble-mailers/#quote-delivery-checks">Prepare a Poly Bubble Quote →</a></div>
    <h2>Measurement and Packing References</h2>
    <p>The BM08 and BM10 examples above use the published <a href="/catalog/Welltroy-Product-Catalog-2025.pdf">Welltroy catalogue</a>; usable inner dimensions are confirmed separately. <a href="https://faqs.clearbags.com/customer-service-questions/how-do-you-measure-usable-space" rel="noopener">ClearBags describes its own inner/usable measurement convention</a>, showing why the stated size basis matters when comparing suppliers.</p>
    <p><a href="https://www.usps.com/ship/packages.htm" rel="noopener">USPS packing guidance</a> recommends suitable packaging, room for cushioning and accurate package measurements. Follow the selected carrier and service requirements for your complete pack; this guide does not establish a transit protection rating.</p>
  </article><aside class="side-card"><p class="eyebrow">Compare actual products</p><h2>Related Mailers</h2><div class="guide-options">
    <a href="/products/yellow-kraft-bubble-mailers/"><strong>Yellow Kraft Bubble Mailers</strong><span>Paper exterior with a bubble lining</span></a>
    <a href="/products/poly-bubble-mailers/"><strong>Poly Bubble Mailers</strong><span>Compare 15 listed outer sizes</span></a>
    <a href="/products/kraft-padded-mailers/"><strong>Kraft Padded Mailers</strong><span>Confirm the proposed lining construction</span></a>
  </div><a class="text-link" href="/guides/choose-a-mailer/">Compare plain and cushioned mailers →</a></aside></div></section>
</Layout>
<style>.bubble-guide-hero{padding-block:52px 44px}.bubble-guide-hero h1{font-size:clamp(2.15rem,4.3vw,3.5rem);line-height:1.16;text-wrap:balance;max-width:1000px}.article-main h2{font-size:clamp(1.65rem,2.8vw,2.1rem);line-height:1.25;text-wrap:balance}.side-card h2{font-size:1.5rem;line-height:1.25}@media(max-width:600px){.bubble-guide-hero{padding-block:34px 30px}.bubble-guide-hero .button{white-space:normal;text-align:center}}.article-main{min-width:0}.article-main td{min-width:145px;vertical-align:top}.article-main li{margin:0 0 10px}h2[id]{scroll-margin-top:120px}</style>
